  {
    "number": 98,
    "title": "Record delivered Nanoleaf Linux source and remaining acceptance",
    "body": "Nanoleaf PR #57 merged as `2558df5a2fc543247b0c75898ef0260ba3ea264b`, all nine PR and nine main jobs passed, and source issue #54 closed. Update canonical architecture, the roadmap and maintained guide to show delivered Linux source and the remaining installed acceptance in Nanoleaf #55. Hub #43 stays open.\n\nRefs #43. This follows [Hub PR #84](https://github.com/jimmie-potts/agent-device-hub/pull/84) and completes the source-status synchronization for [Nanoleaf PR #57](https://github.com/jimmie-potts/codex-nanoleaf/pull/57). It does not install services or publish the public guide.\n\nRefresh complete three-repository backlogs and history, retain #54/#55 acceptance reads, remove closed #54 from open coverage, and mark its roadmap node delivered. Preserve concurrent PC lighting, Prism, CI and guide-checkpoint work. All nine architecture viewers, definitions and source pins remain unchanged because ownership and command flows have not changed. The introduction explains that their dated proposal labels precede Linux source delivery. Installed behavior remains unverified. This status maintenance needs no product OpenSpec change or architecture redraw.\n\nClosing #54 revealed that a maintenance assertion still expected its closed prerequisite in the open-work roadmap. The failing check expected N54 → N55 after N54 closed. Filter expected native blockers to OPEN, matching the adjacent ordering test, while retaining the actual closed dependency in saved GitHub evidence.\n\nValidation:\n\n- Generation, four maintenance tests and browser checks passed. Browser coverage includes six widths from 320 to 1440, all nine viewers, links, coverage, search, navigation, diagram/timeline controls and print restoration, with no page errors. The desktop timeline was inspected.\n- Node 24 setup, workflow validation and thirteen workflow tests passed. Inventory: three specifications and three archived changes.\n- 107 primary open issues, 122 linked issues, 12 guides, 48 roadmap nodes, 65 merged PR records. HTML SHA-256: `6ab5529f887d75edbe9f537477e9bda5992dadff99390583f030d6156604645b`.\n- Complete backlog snapshot: `2026-09-10T23:03:35.592655+00:00`; history read: `2026-09-10T23:03:12.326361+00:00`. Architecture review dates are preserved.\n\nFrozen base/merge-base: `f2b37b6c8db29411e34e8bcf1e73c50c47ff7fe7`. Candidate: `72731eba9428c45c785b5e63856cdc7027c9bb62`. Worktree clean; `git diff --check` passed. Independent Standards and Specification reviews and every configured CI job are required before guarded merge. The existing [guide human-approval exemption](https://github.com/jimmie-potts/agent-device-hub/pull/76#issuecomment-5592944973) applies to this guide maintenance.\n\nPublic currency was checked through its repository README, which still names source `950f7f6` and eight viewers. Public publication and live verification remain pending, outside this source wrap-up.\n",
